<code>assert \result != null && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result.toByteArray().length; \result.toByteArray()[i] == (i < bb.remaining() ? bb.get(i) : 0);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \result != null && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result.toByteArray().length; \result.toByteArray()[i] == bb.array()[bb.position() + i];</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \result != null && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result.toByteArray().length; \result.toByteArray()[i] == (i < bb.remaining() ? bb.get(i) : 0);</code>

However, since the `bb` buffer is sliced and its limit is adjusted, we need to ensure we are comparing against the correct portion of the buffer. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert \result != null && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result.toByteArray().length; \result.toByteArray()[i] == (i < bb.limit() ? bb.get(bb.position() + i) : 0);</code>
--------------------
